toolu_01BMSVzigVu1V5VbUX91ds4H", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 364362, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled payments-worker back to v3.3.0 and opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call. The worker has recovered, but payments-api is still showing errors.\n\n- **Rollback:** The approver signed off, and payments-worker is now on v3.3.0 in us-east, us-west and eu-west. Its error rate fell from 18% to 0.2%, and it reports healthy.\n- **Incident:** The first attempt to open it timed out. I checked that no incident had been created before retrying, and the retry reused the same key so it couldn't make a duplicate.\n- **Still open:** Right after the rollback, payments-api was still on v5.1.0 with an 18% error rate and marked unhealthy. That may just be lag as the worker recovers. If it doesn't come down soon, the API may have its own problem, and rolling it back to v5.0.0 (its last healthy release) would be the next thing to consider. I haven't touched payments-api; tell me if you want me to roll it back.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01HgJ1JTxibP9KHVAvSaAFPt", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_019ZpLbUwcMpGn14YcGBWz8x", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_011YPXiNS4fXQAbBo8uEVgms", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01V2XzVQP2jGKgVVoB8kZhef", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Bwey9jktL1k9SdGKKAeucU", "caller": {"ty