ithout fixing the problem.\n\nWhich do you want?\n1. Roll back **`payments-api`** to v5.0.0 and open a SEV2 incident for it\n2. Roll back **`payments-worker`** to v3.3.0 and open a SEV2 incident for it\n3. Roll back **both** to their last healthy releases and open a SEV2 incident\n\nBoth target versions were healthy in production, so none of these needs change-manager approval. I can run whichever you pick right away.", "type": "text"}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01BuShJ2gjj2eCAau4rDwwJy", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker", "version": "v3.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01T2Er1MTdecNf14DAiqGKAS", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "payments-worker v3.4.0 deploy causing elevated errors; rolled back to v3.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "payments-worker", "summary": "This morning's payments-worker v3.4.0 deploy is unhealthy, with an 18% error rate in us-east, us-west and eu-west. payments-api (v5.1.0, degraded, 18% error rate) is failing as a downstream effect of the worker. Mitigation: rolled payments-worker back to v3.3.0, its last release that was healthy in production. Next: confirm payments-worker and payments-api error rates recover, then find the root cause in v3.4.0.", "idempotency_key": "payments-worker-v3.4.0-rollback-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01Kutd8ZatzLBRUdEkxGKawP", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01DM8S9hZ5jH3WXBuuJYqGdf", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01XAfhfks3kPgNW4FnCsT3hH", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-api"